 "scenery": [],
 "par": {
  "time": 600
 },
 "intro": {
  "title": "LANTERN OSSUARY",
  "lines": [
   "A web of corridors cut in the stone, and every wall is bone.",
   "The oil is what you carry. The dark does not run out."
  ]
 },
 "outro": "The well room opens on a stair, and the stair on a hall that is lit from below.",
 "messages": [
  {
   "id": "start",
   "at": [38, 71],
   "radius": 4,
   "speaker": "INES",
   "text": "Bone for walls, floor to roof, in niches. Not heaped. Stacked, long bones one way and skulls in a row, the way you stack barrels."
  },
  {
   "id": "lamp",
   "at": [38, 68],
   "radius": 3,
   "speaker": "HULL",
   "text": "The lantern is L, an oil a second, a tin is thirty. Gaunts, Gills and Zealots find you by eye: 6 metres in the dark, 24 with the lantern lit. Tollbearers do not care."
  },
  {
   "id": "log1",
   "at": [32, 68],
   "radius": 3,
   "speaker": "PELLEW, MARROW GIRL (LOG)",
   "text": "Day 9 below. Eleven left the beach, six are left. We burn one lantern at a time and keep the rest dark. Nineteen tins. It is cold."
  },
  {
   "id": "log2",
   "at": [8, 45],
   "radius": 3,
   "speaker": "PELLEW, MARROW GIRL (LOG)",
   "text": "Day 12. Six. The dark here is not empty. Two of ours stood in the corridor and would not come on. Lit, they blink. Nine tins."
  },
  {
   "id": "ring",
   "at": [9, 27],
   "radius": 4,
   "speaker": "INES",
   "text": "The ring goes right round and the spokes are the only way off it. Whoever laid this out wanted the way down to be long."
  },
  {
   "id": "log3",
   "at": [21, 26],
   "radius": 3,
   "speaker": "PELLEW, MARROW GIRL (LOG)",
   "text": "Day 15. Three. We took the spiral down because every other turning ends in a niche. Four tins. I have stopped counting the dead in the walls."
  },
  {
   "id": "plate",
   "at": [30, 18],
   "radius": 3,
   "speaker": "RINGING PLATE",
   "text": "Run a nail down it: a count of the stacked. Four thousand and sixty, in this ring. The ring below is shorter."
  },
  {
   "id": "log4",
   "at": [27, 36],
   "radius": 3,
   "speaker": "PELLEW, MARROW GIRL (LOG)",
   "text": "Day 16. One. The oil is out and I am writing by the last of the wick. The well is below me. There is something at the bottom of it that is"
  },
  {
   "id": "well",
   "at": [30, 38],
   "radius": 3,
   "speaker": "INES",
   "text": "She stopped at the top of the spoke. Her lantern is on the floor here, empty, with the wick burned to the stub. I will take the tin she did not need."
  },
  {
   "id": "winchhint",
   "at": [1, 1],
   "radius": 0.1,
   "speaker": "INES",
   "text": "Round the ring, across from where the spoke goes down: a hung lantern, and under it a red lamp on an iron plate set in the bone. That is a lever."
  },
  {
   "id": "sealedhint",
   "at": [36, 34],
   "radius": 3,
   "speaker": "HULL",
   "text": "A plain gate at the bottom of the well, and no handle. If it is shut, a counterweight holds it, and the winch for that is on the inner ring, on the wall across from the spoke."
  },
  {
   "id": "winch",
   "at": [1, 1],
   "radius": 0.1,
   "speaker": "HULL",
   "text": "The winch turns a counterweight somewhere under the floor. Below, a stair has come up out of the well."
  },
  {
   "id": "hollow",
   "at": [38, 7],
   "radius": 3,
   "speaker": "HULL",
   "text": "The outer wall rings hollow in the north, in the one stretch that has no niche cut in it."
  },
  {
   "id": "sealed",
   "at": [38, 3],
   "radius": 3,
   "speaker": "PELLEW, MARROW GIRL (LOG)",
   "text": "Day 10. We sealed the spare tins in the wall for whoever came after, and left the north stretch bare to mark it. Eight tins and a pistol. God keep"
  }
 ],
 "objective": "Go down: round the outer ring, down a spoke, round the middle ring, down again. The exit is at the bottom of the well. Keep the oil",
